 html←{parms}HtmlHeader add;caption;title;docTitle;noIndexing;pageTitle
⍝ Strictly speaking this does not only return a header: it also returns...
⍝ * the DOC type
⍝ * an opening html tag
⍝ * an opening body tag
⍝ * some more stuff shared by all Tatin HTML pages
⍝ ⍺ is optional. When given it must carry exactly two items: (noIndexing pageTitle).
⍝ Two rather than "up to two" on purpose: `1 'X'` is a simple vector while `1 'Foo'` is a
⍝ nested one, so a length-tolerant ⍺ would have to tell those apart and would get a
⍝ one-character page title wrong. Pass '' or ⍬ for an item you have nothing to say about.
⍝ `noIndexing`: pass a 1 for a page that should not be indexed by, say, Google.
⍝ The INI entry "CONFIG:NoIndexing" does the same for every page of the server rather than
⍝ just one, which is what a test or a staging Registry wants. An empty vector means "not
⍝ specified": the INI entry then decides, and with neither a page is indexable.
⍝ `pageTitle`: what this particular page is about, typically the same as its H2, like the
⍝ package ID. It goes in front of the server's own title in <title>, so that browser tabs
⍝ and search results tell the pages apart. Pass '' to let the server's title stand on its
⍝ own, which is what the home page wants.
 (noIndexing pageTitle)←{0<⎕NC ⍵:⍎⍵ ⋄ ⍬ ''}'parms'
 :If 0=≢noIndexing
     noIndexing←0 G.INI.Get'CONFIG:NoIndexing'
 :EndIf
 html←''
 html,←⊂'<!DOCTYPE html>'
 html,←⊂'<html lang="en">'
 html,←⊂'<head>'
 title←⊃G.INI.Get'Config:Title'
⍝ `title` on its own remains the server's title: it is used for the logo further down.
 docTitle←title
 :If 0<≢pageTitle
     docTitle←pageTitle,' - ',title
 :EndIf
 html,←⊂'<title>',(EscapeSpecialChars docTitle),'</title>'
 html,←⊂'<meta charset="UTF-8">'
 html,←⊂'<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">'
 :If noIndexing
     html,←⊂'<meta name="robots" content="noindex">'
 :EndIf
 html,←⊂GetGoogleVerification
 html,←⊂'<link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/Assets/CSS/screen.css" media="screen">'
⍝html,←⊂'<link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/Assets/CSS/print.css" media="screen">'   ⍝ Can be useful for debugging the "Print" CSS
 html,←⊂'<link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/Assets/CSS/print.css" media="print">'
 html,←⊂'<link rel="icon" type="image/x-icon" href="/Assets/img/favicon.ico">'
 html,←FetchBackground G.INI
 html,←⍕¨⊆add
 html,←⊂'<link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/Assets/CSS/screen-tweaks.css" media="screen">'
 html,←⊂'<link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/Assets/CSS/print-tweaks.css" media="print">'
 html,←⊂'</head>'
 html,←⊂'<body>'
 html,←⊂'<div id="my-logo">'
 caption←⊃G.INI.Get'Config:Caption'
 html,←⊂'<a href="/"><img id="logo" src="/Assets/img/tatin.png" title="Link to ',title,' main page" alt="Link to ',title,' main page"></a>'
⍝ The caption goes home as well as the logo does: half the visitors aim at the words rather
⍝ than at the picture, and finding nothing there sends them looking for a "Home" menu item
⍝ that does not exist.
 html,←⊂'<h1><a href="/">',caption,'</a></h1>'
 html,←⊂'</div>'
⍝ The menu goes on every page; see `GetMainMenu` for why.
 html,←GetMainMenu ⍬
 html←,¨html
⍝Done
